# ============================================================================
# SIGNING MATERIAL — never in this repository, private or not.
# The Android release keystore is a credential: the package name is permanently
# bound to it, and anyone holding it can sign updates as this app. A leaked
# password file is the same failure. Belt-and-braces here at the root, in
# addition to guidon-app/.gitignore, so a future re-layout cannot expose them.
# ============================================================================
**/keys/
**/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.pfx
*.p12

# Local session/tool state, not project source
.claude/

# Dependencies and build output (rebuilt by `npm install` / `npm run build`)
**/node_modules/
guidon-app/web/
guidon-app/dist/
guidon-app/src-tauri/target/
guidon-app/android/build/
guidon-app/android/app/build/
guidon-app/android/.gradle/
guidon-app/android/local.properties
guidon-app/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/build/

# Scratch tooling and one-shot audit output. Underscore-prefixed
# guidon-app/tools/*.mjs are throwaway scripts (probes, debug helpers) that
# should never accumulate uncommitted in the tree. The old contrast sweep wrote
# its report here; guidon-app/tools/test-contrast-full.mjs now writes to the OS
# temp folder, so this line only keeps stale local copies out of commits.
GUIDON files/contrast-full-sweep-raw.json

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Brainstorming visual-companion session files (local scratch, not shared)
.superpowers/
